<Base title="Yardwatch terms of service" description="Terms for Yardwatch, my personal camera project.">
  <h1>Yardwatch terms of service</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}.</p>

  <p>
    Yardwatch is my personal, non-commercial project for watching the wildlife around my house with my own Google
    Nest cameras. It is not a service offered to anyone else: I am its only user, and only my Google account signs
    in to it.
  </p>

  <h2>The public sightings page</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/yard/">daily log of animal visits</a> is provided as is, for interest only. The counts come from
    automated descriptions of camera clips and can be wrong. Like the rest of this site's text and figures, it may
    be reused under <a href="https://github.com/AndyFooBlah/andrewbrook-dev/blob/main/LICENSE-CONTENT">CC BY 4.0</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Yardwatch comes with no warranty of any kind, and I accept no liability for anyone's use of this site or the
    sightings data.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    How Yardwatch uses Google data is described in the <a href="/yard/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    I may change these terms at any time by updating this page. Questions: contact me, Andrew Brook, via <a href="https://github.com/AndyFooBlah">GitHub</a> or <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/andrewbrook/">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
